  clock: 6  # d8ef
  nonce: d8ef  # d8ef
  message: "Satisfied by two merged PRs: PR1 (commit fb933138d8, additive) + PR2 (commit b97a8ab723, reconcile), both on dev @af339a8d53. RESOLUTION: visibility now has ONE canonical encoding — the new Symbol.visibility field (public/private/protected/internal/package; # axis: visibility wired into _known_axes via all_known_visibility_levels()), computed once in the finalize _finalize_compute_visibility pass from the highest-priority signal (language modifier > legacy Apex/Clojure meta['visibility'] > Python leading-underscore name > public default), with the deciding signal recorded in meta['visibility_signal']. The two prior disagreeing encodings are reconciled: (1) is_exported = is_exported_old AND (visibility=='public') — visibility is NECESSARY not sufficient; (2) modifiers keeps only non-visibility terms (private/public/pub/exported/external/unexported/protected stripped; re_exported KEPT as it marks the re-export mechanism beyond visibility). The legacy meta['visibility'] key is retired (folded into the field + removed). BEHAVIORAL EVIDENCE: whole-suite 15511 passed, 100% coverage. EMPIRICAL PREMISE CHECK that shaped PR2: a PURE is_exported=visibility=='public' alias would have flipped 22319/38243 self-corpus symbols (58%, 19151 in test files) from not-exported to exported — redefining is_exported from public-API-membership(29%) to language-public(87%) and gutting dead-code roots; the AND-with-visibility keeps public-API semantics and moves only 5 symbols (the src/_foo privates the path heuristic wrongly marked exported). awaits_bakeoff_validation: those 5 is_exported changes shift dead-code/reachability for them + dependents."  # d8ef
